From: Mihawk <mihawk@localhost>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] server,ntdll,kernelbase: ps5: cut Steam startup file and server I/O overhead

Phase 1 fast-Steam runtime optimizations measured against Phase 0 base PS5 baseline:
- server/fd.c: skip redundant ftruncate(0) on empty files in open_fd; skip
  grow_file() no-op when eof == st.st_size in set_fd_eof (eliminates 4.8 ms
  pwrite+ftruncate commits on no-op SetEndOfFile); upgrade ps5_realpath_fast
  from 64-entry linear scan to 128x4 LRU hash cache.
- server/mapping.c: try ftruncate() directly before pwrite+ftruncate in
  grow_file() on PS5.
- server/change.c & server/request.c: only call ps5_change_drain() for
  FS-mutating requests (eliminates ~90k+ kevent() calls per 10 s); raise
  periodic poll floor from 25 ms to 200 ms when EVFILT_VNODE kqueue is active.
- server/file.c: 64 KiB buffered read in pw_sd_load() and coalesced single
  write() in pw_sd_set().
- server/process.h & server/request.c: raise child FD leases 32->48 per
  process and 96->120 total (safely under PW_FDV_HIGH_WATER=150).
- server/registry.c & dlls/ntdll/unix/registry.c: 512 KiB stdio buffering in
  save_branch() and save_registry_branch().
- dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c: raise WB_ENTRIES 4->16 and WB_HCACHE 256->512, add
  basename-hash filtering in wb_flush_path() so unrelated NtCreateFile/NtOpenFile/
  NtQueryAttributesFile calls do not shatter write coalescing, and handle cache in
  wb_flush_handle() to skip redundant server_get_unix_fd() RPCs.
- dlls/kernelbase/process.c: clear CREATE_NEW_CONSOLE and set CREATE_NO_WINDOW on
  `run` process rules so SteamService -> hostname.exe skips spawning conhost.exe.

